Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "FallingObjectOnRoadway" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :EvidenceBasedAnomaly ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1 ;
    :hasEvidence :indicator1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :night1 ;
    :occursInScene :scene1 .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Hay bale falling into the path of the vehicle" .

:indicator1 a :FallingObjectIndicator ;
    :description "A large object is airborne and dropping onto the traffic lane" ;
    :indicatesPotentialRisk :risk1 .

:night1 a :NightCondition .

:risk1 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "High risk of collision with a falling obstacle on the road" ;
    :confidenceScore "0.95"^^xsd:float ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.90"^^xsd:float .

Identified Risks for each risk class
Risk 1:
Description: Potential collision with a heavy falling object (hay bale) that is entering the vehicle's driving path.
Severity Score: 0.90